{"title":"2025 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> be positive reals such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e15f9d478363c5f25b7268958b394bbaeb1fde2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 + b^3 = ab + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa01a5b54a72afe6746f547390e65dbbb82ea64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2 + a + b \\geq 2\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28By_Junfei.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(By_Junfei)\">Solution 1 (By Junfei)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (By Junfei)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equation given has a highest degree of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is difficult to handle. Furthermore, by expanding the the equation given and the inequality required,\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35bc59952e02bf0a1099d32d8431d2c02635c183.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+b)(a^2-ab+b^2)=ab+1\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b7720021fe323e434d8c138034cad63e1f994fec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+b^2-2ab+a+b\\geq{2}\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nwe can notice that some elements, such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> (note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf669d58fbd0410ca860758e53606d06425a4d97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> can be formed by the combination of the previous two), have appeared multiple times. A possible approach is substitution, which may turn the expressions much simpler and remove the terms with degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b6170bb32fcbd158e5f1d1ef3f6281a87d4ce497.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bc525d0573fc087cbb2a4cb5488e64c061615ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />. Both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are real numbers greater or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e1b87c1c8490cd6d9b00ea2e136a2f779d76a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=x^2-2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe given equality becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33fbb2b47ba75e69526980903c1081c62577f776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x^2-3y)=y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe inequality we need to prove becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2cf96796b78a715bba43e791c66e0f969eb8935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-4y+x\\geq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSince all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />'s in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33fbb2b47ba75e69526980903c1081c62577f776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x^2-3y)=y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" /> have only degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it is easy to express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and plug this expression into the inquality we need to prove.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33fbb2b47ba75e69526980903c1081c62577f776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x^2-3y)=y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/5782985f381c11602580581dfa340680d9960330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-3xy=y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/8103f3a70ffda003c89e36b41eaec625a5931ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-1=y+3xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568222ffe08bcde1fcba023e7a93dae37a6aef5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{x^3-1}{3x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe inequality we need to prove is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea8a3b97a78d2117cd2dc6ff9b34d324a19db772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />·<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/f/d3f340db7df8a04420a71037612876249f241aaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^3-1}{3x+1}+x\\geq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"123\" height=\"42\" />. This can be simplified by multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c600d96217a56031c04ec7a9cfcf4546eb2a22a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, which is always a positive number.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4049013131aef15470b044ff11b6e60004ebf62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2(3x+1)-4(x^3-1)+x(3x+1)\\geq{2(3x+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"375\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/b/7cb43d792a2bed0adcf0bb08d0f436d0d3f4a801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^3+x^2-4x^3+4+3x^2+x\\geq{6x+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"306\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8b3202f551e6f8d979b78772c29965011862c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^3+4x^2-5x+2\\geq{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"189\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe can notice that, in the original inequality, the inputs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31c3c1ac08dfcd7c59d26c04eb5895f632293d9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0,b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec816753425931dd61b7d7a64a1c91bac0aa1c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1,b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> give us two equality cases. In the first case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffa070d77bf858a379df6b8e7b3b375f89556d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a+b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />, and in the second case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. By dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fadfdcded049849b00382d1f4d5021ed7196b44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^3+4x^2-5x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/74207b77f1ae2a65e1d71cabf58c81d4e5bc9433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)(x-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />, we obtain a quotient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebe4bf9c2b96ee54aa7d3e792caf208b6619a5fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2d4ab1cac5f6cfbe38eb687c377c3d66aa35b39.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-x^3+4x^2-5x+2=(x-1)(x-2)(1-x)=-(x-1)^2(x-2)\\]\" width=\"500\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nBut this is not enough to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8b3202f551e6f8d979b78772c29965011862c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^3+4x^2-5x+2\\geq{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"189\" height=\"19\" />! What if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />? <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a997529821f13142bf807ea9d7dafd5441dc6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(x-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" /> will be negative, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04854d8381ed4ccf9eff2a54ea58b2059b8a454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> will be positive, resulting in a negative product.\n</p><p><br />\nTo resolve this quandary, we would have to review our definitions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c64c92f951891ae17a798629475d8b3c2d25142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dcd30c3fc84a378da46a6dcf3db1992d204fd82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />. There actually exist restrictions for the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. By AM-GM Inequality, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6d1dc48b29097f4ff1de0311397554f5ba3ce52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+b\\geq 2\\sqrt{ab}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503cda4785ab4e007265ae5ae27778ae69f29165.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\geq 2\\sqrt{y}\\]\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568222ffe08bcde1fcba023e7a93dae37a6aef5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{x^3-1}{3x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"42\" />, we obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/57020afbd08b690da76c3381a15ddbeadcf70338.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\geq 2\\sqrt{\\frac{x^3-1}{3x+1}}\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165d672c197575d3e1fbb439ab8610eef86f8ba8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2\\geq 4\\cdot\\frac{x^3-1}{3x+1}\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028ef9ce6b18229ca70fe6a39024a7bf0608536a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2(3x+1)\\geq 4(x^3-1)\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce77b32c638e7608eb9e024e22332dad5d1fcc62.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x^3+x^2\\geq 4(x^3-1)\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d134423a8e9090c7adff48041e156e33508681b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x^3+x^2\\geq 4x^3-4\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc39b42034960ba45a8f7f2fab7d763cf46193a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2\\geq{x^3-4}\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThis gives a bound for the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Lemma:</i>\n</p><p><br />\nFor a non-negative real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc39b42034960ba45a8f7f2fab7d763cf46193a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2\\geq{x^3-4}\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Proof:</i>\n</p><p><br />\nThe inequality is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd0da8ea54a786d80cc967847ea46bba0d1bc23c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4\\geq{x^2(x-1)}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The right-hand side is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/4021beb8c330657cd07e634289eca5426768f4b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2\\times{(2-1)}=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"21\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820c190d962281aa2f9f8050cf0b21209c1a8653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f4f16c134202e1fe413feb1f92a692b02764370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq{x}\\leq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ee5e07ec6635c1290961317e0de410252573fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^3+4x^2-5x+2=-(x-1)^2(x-2)\\geq{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"347\" height=\"21\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2cf96796b78a715bba43e791c66e0f969eb8935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-4y+x\\geq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />. This completes the proof.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\nThe author's extension:\n</p><p><br />\nWith a few extra steps, we can calculate all the equality cases for this problem.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6ddbc427322c3a53a1ae6d140c0fe6ad3e0df0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^3+4x^2-5x+2=(x-1)(x-2)(1-x)=-(x-1)^2(x-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"505\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><br />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4a911219caac7a600cd97b5656f63d8b5faf718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\neq{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63dea127595f88dd36892ba85530615feca8d3f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\neq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/438846d6ff7e63b08c44af2fd5d35502de1176d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(x-1)^2(x-2)\\neq{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe only possibilities for equality are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nRecall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568222ffe08bcde1fcba023e7a93dae37a6aef5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{x^3-1}{3x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIn the first case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/6227e0c2730af45a4f1b7e2ea8d50340b12fb5c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42d8661b2bdfd67d5efbd15b7a06ad95e06a4a93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=0$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>One of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The other one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If we change the problem's restriction from \"positive real numbers\" to \"non-negative real numbers\", <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7372a2f6167ca6f7e7a2bb7d5327f13c40d1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0, b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/077804ce4e27bf17cd94bea69b102309859f90d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1, b=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> are two equality cases.\n</p><p><br />\nIn the second case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/77842bf424059df95ad41ab26b5c7b41452efb8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{2^3-1}{3\\times{2}+1}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"145\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d34205c3f3f6d69729aae95da801385bc3a91b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=2, ab=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c47404f7183b64ae1085aad39e4a342c4114ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{1}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bb6f28f42a76e8bd6945221971d6a50992ae0f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+\\frac{1}{b}=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/9/579f0dc9385da31121ef583d03a181244f186ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2-2b+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf590e9abb33aa9776ddc386b1ba6ee7b43fa413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/6/9e69164f505ed21796ab3f57a6affdca2dc2c27e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> is the third equality case.\n</p><p><br />\nAll the possible equality cases have been found.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033843\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 311/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17784/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36740:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018033843 and revision id 283633. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}